# UNO CLI Extension Readiness Report

## Overview

This document evaluates how prepared the refactored UNO CLI project is for future extensions and feature additions.

The refactoring process significantly improved the project structure, making the codebase more adaptable for continued development.

---

# Current Extension Readiness

The project is now moderately to highly extension-ready due to improvements in:

* modularity
* readability
* logic separation
* reduced duplication
* cleaner gameplay flow

These changes make it easier to implement new features without heavily modifying existing systems.

---

# Areas Improved for Extensibility

## 1. Simplified Gameplay Flow

Turn management and gameplay progression are now easier to follow and modify.

This supports future additions such as:

* custom turn rules
* timed turns
* tournament modes
* online synchronization

---

## 2. Reusable Helper Methods

Extracted helper methods allow new features to reuse existing logic instead of duplicating code.

Examples:

* card validation
* player switching
* card drawing
* deck reshuffling

Benefits:

* lower implementation complexity
* fewer future bugs

---

## 3. Centralized Rule Logic

Special card handling is now more centralized.

This allows easier implementation of:

* custom cards
* house rules
* stacking rules
* additional penalties
* alternate wild card behaviors

---

## 4. Cleaner Data Management

Improved handling of:

* player hands
* deck state
* discard pile
* scores

makes future persistence and networking features easier to implement.

---

